# Archify Skill Rule

When the user asks to "archify", "show project structure", or "analyze architecture", generate an updated directory tree and structural overview.

Rules:
1. Ignore common build/dependency folders (e.g., node_modules, .git, Library, Temp, Logs, obj, bin, Build, .vs).
2. Format directory structure using clean ASCII/Markdown tree syntax.
3. Group core modules by their structural role (e.g., Core, Systems, Managers, UI, Utilities).
4. Briefly list key entry points and component responsibilities alongside the tree layout.